 "id": "2026-10-09-spacex-spectrum-telecoms",
 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "SpaceX just bought a slice of America's airwaves. The next day, the country's three phone giants sold off hard."
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "On Thursday, SpaceX, the rocket and Starlink company, agreed to buy nationwide low-band spectrum from the investment firm Grain Management. The Wall Street Journal puts the price at about 8 billion dollars. The deal still needs approval from the FCC."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "On Friday, T-Mobile closed down 13.3 percent, AT&T 9.8 and Verizon 8.8, Axios reports. Cell tower owners like Crown Castle jumped instead, as investors bet on SpaceX as a future tenant of their towers."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Why the panic? Low-band signals reach indoors, where satellite signals struggle. SpaceX plans a phone service for late 2027, with small base stations next to Starlink dishes. Its president has said she expects to win quite a few carrier customers. AT&T's CEO calls the plan not viable."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Follow for the next update."
  }
 ],
